<title>JAPAN: Australia's WATC launches 5.2% yen/Aussie samurai.</title>
<headline>Australia's WATC launches 5.2% yen/Aussie samurai.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following yen/Australian dollar dual-currency samurai bond issue was announced by lead-manager Nomura Securities on Wednesday:</p>
<p> BORROWER	  Western Australian Treasury Corp (WATC)</p>
<p> AMT		 40 bln yen</p>
<p> COUPON	    5.2 pct</p>
<p> ISS PRICE	 par</p>
<p> MATURITY	  13 May 1999</p>
<p> PAY DATE	  13 May 1997</p>
<p> SUB PERIOD	May 1 to May 9</p>
<p> PAY FREQ	  Semi-annual</p>
<p> LAST RATING     S&amp;P AA, Moody's Aa2</p>
<p> LEAD MANAGER    Nomura Securities</p>
<p> LEAD TRUSTEE    Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi</p>
<p>NOTE: The exchange rate was fixed at A$5,031.19 per 500,000 yen. -- Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-3432-8785</p>
</text>
